WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.170
Encore! Encore! Encore!

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:02.980
Jumpei!

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.700
<i>We will now have the award ceremony</i>

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.410
<i>announcing the MVP for 
the 79th Ballet Festival.</i>

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.450
It's definitely the Rothbart 
boy, don't you think?

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.250
I want him and the prince to both win!

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.000
<i>This is Special Judge Oikawa Ayako-san, Artistic 
Director of the Oikawa Haruka Ballet Company.</i>

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.640
Godai-sensei used to be part of the 
Oikawa Haruka Ballet Company, right?

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:39.390
Yes, we enrolled at Godai Ballet Studio 
because of its connections to Oikawa.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.890
<i>Today's MVP is...</i>

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:47.080
<i>Kawasaki Misono-san 
from Takara Ballet Studio.</i>

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:47.820
Good job!

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.900
<i>Congratulations.</i>

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:48.900
Congrats!

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.650
What? It's not one of the boys?

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.280
Congratulations, Kawasaki-san.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.910
Your splendid performance 
was worthy of the MVP.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:02.790
However,

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:07.840
there was unfortunately one school 
whose performance and attitude

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.040
could hardly be called "ballet."

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.320
On top of that, to respond 
to the call for an encore...

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.300
I deeply apologize for their behavior.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:18.880
Why?!

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.810
The audience liked us the best!

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:28.440
What is your name?

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.810
I'm Murao Jumpei!

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.950
Murao-kun, I'm afraid I don't 
understand why you're here.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.700
Ballet is an art.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:45.830
That impromptu spectacle by your school 
and the attitude accompanying it

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.460
is something inherently different 
from classical ballet.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:50.770
What?

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.470
No one who claims with a straight
 face that what they do is "art"

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.600
is ever actually any good!

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:01.100
I do not think you are suited to ballet.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.610
You should try a different kind of dance.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.990
<b>Godai Ballet Studio
 Dressing Room</b>

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.940
Act 6: "Why Am I Doing Ballet?"

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.620
Thanks to you changing the choreography,

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.110
the judges lumped me together with you!

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.910
Oikawa Ayako was right.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.380
You should quit ballet.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:53.670
What?!

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.750
Okay, okay.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.160
It's true that if Jumpei hadn't
 changed the choreography,

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:00.140
Luou might've been the MVP.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:04.860
But then we wouldn't have been 
able to see your true dancing.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:11.340
My goal is to dance in a competition!

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.990
Well, a promise is a promise.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:17.870
Luou!

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.820
Huh? Competition?

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.080
I promised that if he got MVP,

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.690
I'd arrange for him to compete 
in an overseas competition.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:26.340
Huh?

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.610
Chizuru-sensei!

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.670
What is the meaning of this?!

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.680
Did you hear what Oikawa-san said?

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.110
The choreography...

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.150
The girls had less time on stage.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.220
They practiced so hard, too...

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:38.950
Um...

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.720
I'm sorry, that was my—

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:41.420
Jumpei!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:46.220
Take the younger ones to 
the lobby with Miyako.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.370
Oh, thanks!

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.610
Sorry you couldn't dance that much.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:55.270
It's okay.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.000
No worries!

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.190
We were in the encore.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:03.040
Jumpei-kun was in all 
of the classes, wasn't he?

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:06.540
I was concerned about his 
special treatment before.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.200
If he continues to study at your school,

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.200
I will be withdrawing my daughter.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:15.950
I understand.

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:19.000
I will make sure he does not join 
the classes in the future.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:23.640
However, I cannot make him quit.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.690
I have a responsibility

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.220
as the one who discovered him.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.350
Huh?

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.370
Hyou-chan!

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:36.230
What're you doing here?

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:38.980
The soccer club training camp is today.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.980
Oh, something happened with the club, huh?

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.510
I knew it! I mean, you can 
be a real pain sometimes.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:48.410
The hell?!

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:51.370
Thanks.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.390
For shouting my name back there.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:06:01.750
That ballet crowd you've gotten involved 
with looks like a huge headache.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.980
Right?

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:06.410
After being told all that...

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.080
I mean, what does "not suited" mean, anyway?

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.950
I don't think I know what "ballet" is, then.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:13.740
But...

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.250
It was interesting.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.900
You know, your mic work.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.620
What about my dancing?!

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.400
You'll be okay.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:26.240
In ballet or whatever else you do.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.490
Just be yourself.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.360
That "art lady," too...

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.330
She's mad 'cause she's scared.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.600
Drag her into it.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:45.590
<b>Oikawa Haruka Ballet Company 
</b>Tokyo-based ballet company

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:45.590
<b></b>The Oikawa Haruka Ballet Company 
is a ballet company in Tokyo.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:45.590
<b>Oikawa Ayako</b>

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:47.620
<i>What's the "ballet" Ayako was talking about?</i>

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.300
<b>Invited by Brute Lee</b>

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.300
<b>Director
 Takehara Naoto</b>

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.300
<b>Fukiishi Kazuko</b>

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.300
<b>Mito Yukino</b>

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.300
<b>Starring Natsuji Akio</b>

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.300
<b>Stunt Coordinator
 Murao Ippeita</b>

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.540
<i>That was amazing...</i>

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.310
<i>That sparkle... and "boom!"</i>

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.600
<i>Sorry, but I couldn't help but
 think to myself, "I can't die here."</i>

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.790
<i>It's not about the basics.</i>

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:09.830
<i>It's what I was drawn to.</i>

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:11.520
<i>What I believed in.</i>

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:15.780
<i>If the essence of what I'm 
aiming for isn't ballet, then...</i>

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:20.250
Why am I doing ballet?

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.960
What?! Most of the younger kids withdrew?!

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:28.410
Oh, you told him.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.510
He would've figured it out eventually.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:33.140
The girls from the 14-and-up class, too...

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:35.220
Jumpei?

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:41.730
<i>It appears Godai-sensei will not stop 
giving you special treatment,</i>

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:47.980
and I'd enrolled my daughter to help her 
get chosen as an Oikawa special student,

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.570
<i>but if Oikawa Ayako 
isn't happy with the school,</i>

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.570
<i>then there's no point.</i>

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.370
<i>All right!</i>

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.490
I get it! I'll...

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.700
Drag her into it.

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:04.610
...make Oikawa Ayako acknowledge me!

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.210
Luou!

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.590
What the hell's that stretch? 
Teach it to me later.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.250
But first, look at this!

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.100
I found it yesterday!

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.970
<b>Oikawa Haruka Ballet School</b>

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.970
<b>Boys Summer Class</b>

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.970
<b>Taking applications</b>

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.970
<b></b>~This summer, you'll be the hottest!~

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.970
<b><b>8 days of intensive classes</b></b>

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.970
Oikawa Haruka Ballet 
School's Boys Summer Class!

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:17.820
And guess what? It starts today!

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.350
On the last day, you perform 
the variation you practiced

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.030
and get critiqued by Oikawa Ayako herself!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.100
Yeah, no... I don't want to go!

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:29.000
This has nothing to do with me. 
You can just go by yourself!

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.370
It <i>does</i> have to do with you.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:34.110
You were frustrated, right? 
Enough to bang on the wall.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.230
We'll make her acknowledge us!

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:41.000
What the heck?

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.870
Ballet must be pretty lucrative...

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:46.760
<b>Boys Summer Class</b>

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.690
<b></b>~This summer, you'll be the hottest!~

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.120
<b>Taking applications</b>

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:49.410
<b>Class Full 
Applications Closed</b>

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:49.790
Well, applications are closed, though.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:50.170
<b><b>Critique by Oikawa Ayako 
on the last day!</b></b>

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:50.170
<b>Full of amazing instructors!!</b>

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:50.170
<b></b>You'll be taught by pro dancers!⭐︎

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:54.420
<b>Oikawa Haruka Ballet</b>

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:53.120
Is that what it says?

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.120
Huh?

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:00.440
Himenokouji Kotobuki-kun.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:02.450
His family comes from old wealth,

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:06.020
and his parents are passionate 
supporters of the company.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:11.690
As you can see, his ballet technique, 
sensibilities, and ability are...

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:16.060
Having a supportive family is also 
an important part of talent.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.370
Oh, that tall boy...

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:19.970
Right.

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:25.640
That's Takura Yamato, who won second place 
at the Japan Ballet Competition.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:30.000
He's already 180 centimeters tall 
as a third-year in junior high.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.910
He's also very skilled.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:34.190
Those leg muscles...

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:36.720
I wonder how much of them he can shed.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:39.950
And of course, everyone's 
eyes are drawn to...

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:43.380
Yasuda Misaki-kun, 
someone you've also noticed.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.490
I have nothing but praise for his talents.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:53.600
He wishes to join the SS class here 
and continue at his home school in Kyoto.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:57.860
However, his teacher in 
Kyoto is against it...

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:02.700
Well, I'll try speaking to his teacher.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:05.750
Can I leave the rest to you?

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.210
Very well.

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:08.970
Did you know?

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:12.680
Being placed in the spot 
right in front of the mirror

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.090
is a requirement for being 
scouted as a special student.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:20.340
Everyone, please go to your place 
at the barre when I tell you to.

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:23.600
Starting in front of the mirror 
from the piano side...

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.850
Kotobuki-kun.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.100
Misaki-kun.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:27.580
Yamato-kun.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.860
I am your instructor, Nakamura.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:37.610
All of you here are studying 
at various studios.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:43.120
However, for the next eight days, 
please give the Oikawa way a try.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.120
I hope the next eight days

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:54.880
will be an opportunity for you all to 
relearn precisely what classical ballet is.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.580
Now, in eight days—

00:10:56.580 --> 00:11:00.760
See? If we look like we know where 
we're going, no one will try to stop us!

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.140
What are you two doing?

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.600
Oikawa Ayako-san!

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:15.980
I'm here because I want to know 
what it is you call "ballet"!

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:20.900
Please teach me what "art" is!

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.520
Nakamura-sensei.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:25.330
Yes?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.980
These boys will be joining the class.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:27.910
H-Huh?!

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:30.330
Put them both in front of the mirror.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:35.420
I'm looking forward to the last day.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.050
Ayako-sensei!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:41.130
What? That was too easy...

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:42.450
Huh?

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:44.620
Luou?

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:50.930
Make sure you do a thorough 
background check on those two.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.680
I'm going to take both of them.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:01.900
I'm Murao Jumpei, currently studying 
at the Godai Ballet Studio!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.240
I've been doing ballet for...

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.370
Let's see...

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.160
Three months!

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:08.790
Three months?

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:12.790
Do you mean that's how long you've 
been at Godai-sensei's studio?

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.480
What about before that?

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.050
I did a martial art called Jeet Kune Do.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:21.850
I see.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:23.870
What about you?

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:28.260
Mori... Luou...

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.390
My grandmother... taught me...

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.150
Huh? What did you say?

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:36.410
<i>Why is he going into bullied kid mode?</i>

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:40.150
<i>What am I going to do with these two?</i>

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:44.420
<i>Did Ayako-san choose them just 
because of their raw talent?</i>

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.560
<i>He has not only the right build, 
but a pretty face, too...</i>

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:53.270
<i>And look at the feet on the one who 
doesn't seem to know anything about ballet!</i>

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:54.580
<i>Those feet!</i>

00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:57.720
Sorry I'm late.

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:00.500
The class before this ran late.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:04.420
I'm the pianist, Tsumamura.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:05.510
What?!

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.180
<i>Piano?</i>

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.680
<i>Live accompaniment?</i>

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.680
Now then, let us begin the class.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.090
Reverence.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.690
<i>Oh?</i>

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:36.240
Now, we will start by facing the barre.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.910
Stand in a tight first position and...

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:41.250
Devant, and close...

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.210
Music, please.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:51.720
<i>I knew it! She makes shiny drops of sound!</i>

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:00.920
Hey, you should be able to 
remember this much, at least!

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.730
At the center, I'll be giving you 
even longer enchaînements!

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:14.330
Jumpei! You're not in time with the music!

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:15.600
Huh?!

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:16.830
Listen carefully.

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:18.820
<i>What?</i>

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.270
<i>I was off?</i>

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:26.090
<i>No one's ever said I wasn't in time 
with the music before!</i>

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:34.350
<i>Oh, this is from </i>The Piano<i>!</i>

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.500
<i>And with this arrangement!</i>

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.120
You're off!

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:44.880
How many times must I tell you?!

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:47.260
Listen to the music!

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:48.410
<i>I'm listening!</i>

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:50.500
<i>I'm totally listening!</i>

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:55.160
You're not listening to 
what I'm saying, either!

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.540
Why are you tilting your head?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.980
What? Was I doing that?

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:02.840
Jumpei, go to the back.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.230
Everyone in this row, move forward.

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:08.130
Damn, he sure dropped fast.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:12.920
Luou, you keep looking down. 
You're not focused at all.

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.350
Go to the back.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:19.730
Now, we will go to the center, 
but before that,

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:20.410
You know, this isn't school.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:23.650
since it's the first day, 
it looks like you're all a bit nervous,

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:23.650
If you got serious, you could blow 
everyone out of the water.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.730
and your movements are stiff.

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:31.780
Hey. Did you notice that the guys in front 
of the mirror are the best dancers?

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.750
Oh, but the tall guy that switched with you

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:39.540
and that cool kid who kept his spot 
in front of the mirror...

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.260
They might be better than you.

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:45.470
Well, I'll get my spot back before you,

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:48.560
so you can keep being scared that you're 
not at your home studio and stay here.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:52.400
I'll get Ayako's acknowledgment 
for both of us!

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.560
Shut up, wild monkey.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.500
All right, let's get our spots back.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.710
Plié, and step!

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:07.380
Promenade.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.480
Pull up your knees.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:23.300
<i>Just how competitive is he?</i>

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.320
<i>He was trembling a minute ago.</i>

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:28.300
Turn.

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:36.430
Stop and hold that position. Lift your legs.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.350
Luou, wonderful!

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:40.850
<i>I can't lose, either.</i>

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.380
Jumpei! You're off again!

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:44.920
Listen to the music!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.680
Plié, fondu to the side, 
step onto that foot,

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:52.640
coupé to the back with a half-turn.

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:53.890
One more time.

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:55.330
Fondu side, half-turn...

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.540
Jumpei.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:01.470
Those hand movements. You're not 
marking the steps, are you?

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:06.480
Everyone marks the foot movements 
with their hands to remember them.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.650
What, really?!

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:11.380
Wait, what were ya doin', then?

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.380
Were you just doing what 
everyone else was doing?

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.900
No, he's only been dancing for three months.

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.670
You might be off because 
you can't remember the steps

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.140
and aren't sure about the movements.

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:25.310
<i>No, I know what the moves are...</i>

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:29.020
<i>But it's off from the image I have in my mind.</i>

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:31.730
Well?

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:35.480
Wh-Who did you say was better than me?

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:37.990
The contrast between what you 
say and how you act is intense!

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.490
That guy's toes aren't pointed enough.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.520
That guy's not turned out.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.750
They all had shaky landings.

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:52.210
They're all barely keeping up with 
the music. Worse than you, in a way.

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:59.780
Jumpei, prioritize fine 
positioning over the acting!

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:03.050
Jumpei! Hurry up and get in place!

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:04.300
R-Right!

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:10.760
<i>One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.</i>

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:15.170
<i>One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.</i>

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:19.640
<i>One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.</i>

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:24.080
<i>One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight!</i>

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.600
See? You can do it!

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.520
You were on this time!

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:29.940
Wh-What?

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:32.840
I just ignored the music 
and counted while I danced...

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:37.190
That means ya matched the rhythm 
and danced to the music, right?

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.740
Ya weren't ignorin' it.

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:39.770
Jumpei.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:42.720
You're not at that point yet.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.870
Just keep count when you're dancing.

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:51.230
<i>Then... it won't feel good!</i>

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:54.420
"This is so damn boring!"

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:59.280
That was the expression on your face 
during the second half of class.

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.840
I like your piano playing.

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:04.620
Thanks.

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.120
When you dance, you don't just 
try to follow the rhythm.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:11.620
You can't help but try to express 
the emotions of the music, too.

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:14.840
All without realizing it.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.630
Is that bad?

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:19.800
Come with me.

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:23.910
This is Oikawa's SS class.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:28.280
Only students qualified to become 
professionals are in this class.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:32.230
Oh, it happens to be a boys' class.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.780
So cool!

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:43.800
It's like synchronized dancing.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:45.810
Don't you think so?

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:49.300
All their movements are perfectly 
and beautifully in sync.

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:51.280
I feel like I'm watching a performance.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.260
This is exactly what 
"ballet" should look like.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:20:00.380
They're the complete opposite of you, 
dancing to "feel good."

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.060
<i>But...</i>

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:04.170
<i>If they're so together like that,</i>

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:06.670
<i>I'm sure it feels really good to them, too!</i>

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:08.800
How do you think they can be so together?

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.650
Unlike in other classes,

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:17.320
the SS class does the same 
enchaînement for a month.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:22.640
By repeating it, they don't have to 
think about what the steps are,

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:26.610
and they can focus on moving 
their bodies precisely.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:31.580
In other words, the basics can 
completely permeate their bodies.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.890
They look so together

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:38.340
because they've all arrived at the same 
goal of the ideal movement.

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:42.150
<i>This is... "art"!</i>

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:44.710
You have good sensibilities.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.960
For example, you <i>were</i> in
 time with the music earlier.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:47.760
What?

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:52.830
The ability to get lost in the music 
is a wonderful talent.

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.580
Then why was I forced to keep count?

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:58.360
Why isn't what I do "ballet"?!

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:01.840
Still, the music and emotions...

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:05.530
That explosion of light...

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:11.680
I thought getting carried away 
by all that was "ballet."

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.310
No, I know.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:18.480
It all comes down

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:22.290
to how I'm not good enough at the basics 
to worry about that other stuff, right?

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:23.900
I know that!

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:27.720
I'm in more of a hurry than I expected,

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:30.560
after watching them...

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:35.050
You're right. Without the basics, 
everything else is out of the question.

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:38.160
But before all that, 
it looks like you're too unaware

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:41.820
of your own dancing and 
your attitude toward "ballet."

00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:43.820
What do you mean?

00:21:44.270 --> 00:21:48.390
When you dance, everything 
inside you comes radiating out.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:50.830
It's so scary.

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:52.950
Reflect a bit on what you're doing,

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.520
or you might not be able to 
get to where they are.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:59.830
<i>Well, it's not like I'm trying 
to join the SS class.</i>

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:02.090
Huh?

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:09.210
Sorry! I didn't think you wouldn't 
know how to ride the train!

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:11.490
I'll go pick you up tomorrow, too.

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:12.400
I'm not going.

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:13.200
Huh?

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:17.010
Once Ayako acknowledges you, you can 
talk to Chizuru-san about competing—

00:22:17.010 --> 00:22:17.980
I don't care anymore.

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:24.160
Sorry.

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:27.490
I didn't realize you'd have a hard time 
in a place with so many guys our age.

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:30.710
Reflect a bit on what you're doing.

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:35.000
<i>If I'd thought about it, would I have 
been able to figure it out?</i>

00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:41.000
I didn't know about you needing 
to get MVP to compete, either.

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:43.380
If you had, would you have 
stuck to the choreography?

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:46.210
<i>No... I wouldn't have...</i>

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:49.110
<i>I mean, I thought that I couldn't die.</i>

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:53.180
<i>Yeah, who would've wanted to see 
the cool but boring Rothbart</i>

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:56.640
<i>with a prince who was only 
worried about the basics?</i>

00:22:57.230 --> 00:22:59.390
<i>I saw Luou at the gym.</i>

00:22:59.710 --> 00:23:02.280
<i>I thought he'd kill me 
with that same spirit,</i>

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:04.570
<i>and he did even better than that!</i>

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:07.150
<i>And then the audience loved it!</i>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:10.030
Luou...

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:12.590
Sorry...

00:23:12.590 --> 00:23:14.580
for relying on you back then.

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:18.860
I was completely unaware 
of anything about ballet.

00:23:18.860 --> 00:23:21.250
I didn't know anything... I was arrogant...

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:23.840
I prioritized "feeling good" 
over everything else...

00:23:26.190 --> 00:23:31.580
I-I'm so embarrassed... so please 
come with me tomorrow, too!

00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:32.590
Okay?

00:23:33.270 --> 00:23:34.220
No way!

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:35.890
<b><i>Preview</i></b>

00:23:36.230 --> 00:23:38.140
She saw right through my audacity...

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:39.520
<b>Arghhhhh!</b>

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:42.890
I thought I could overcome the difference 
between us with my sensibilities...

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:48.350
<i>Dance Dance Danseur</i>, Act 7: 
"Ah, I'm So Embarrassed."

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:49.900
Act 7 
"Ah, I'm So Embarrassed"
